  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1980-p27.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the two real cube roots be \\(u\\) and \\(v.\\) Then \\[ \\begin{aligned} uv&=\\sqrt[3]{25-52}=-3,\\\\ u^3+v^3&=10. \\end{aligned} \\] If \\(t=u+v,\\) then \\(t^3=10-9t,\\) so \\[ \\begin{gathered} t^3+9t-10\\\\ =(t-1)(t^2+t+10)\\\\ =0. \\end{gathered} \\] The only real solution is \\(t=1,\\) which is not listed.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Call the two cube roots \\(u\\) and \\(v\\), and compute \\(uv\\)",
        "Use \\((u+v)^3=u^3+v^3+3uv(u+v)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
